      "text": "To determine the product of the two numbers given that their least common multiple (LCM) is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we can use the relationship between the LCM and the GCD of two numbers. That relationship is as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\na \\times b = 36 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nTo find the product, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
